5.
Explain in 3-4 lines how using a virtual environment (venv) helps when working on multiple automation projects, especially if you need different package versions for each.
Answer:

A venv keeps each project separate.
Each project can have different package versions.
It stops packages from causing problems with each other.
It makes projects easy to manage.

